{"alias":"/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/manual/chronic","title":"Guidelines for School Health Services: Chronic Conditions Management","changed":"2026-09-16T15:38:34+00:00","before":"<p><img alt=\"School Health - Chronic Conditions Web Banner\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"d1696075-98ae-45bc-abac-5b9dd7a4fe82\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/School%20Health%20-%20Chronic%20Conditions%20Web%20Banner.png\" width=\"100%\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Students with chronic conditions often have unique educational needs and health considerations that require individual planning. Every student with a chronic condition should have access to school nursing care. Better management and control of chronic health conditions are key, leading to success for these students, both in school and in their community. Care for these students should include teaching and encouraging self-care skills, as the locus of control for making decisions about health shifts to the individual.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To help schools eliminate discrimination against students with disabilities due to chronic conditions or other reasons, the Office of Civil Rights created this resource: <a href=\"https://www.ed.gov/media/document/parent-and-educator-resource-guide-section-504-public-elementary-and-secondary-schools-2016-21262.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Parent and Educator Guide to Section 504</a>. Many students with chronic conditions will qualify for accommodations through Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-12\">\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary mb-3\"><strong>Chronic Conditions Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://cdn.fs.pathlms.com/GtkmrVvSy64YFX7jL4Yh?cache=true\">School Wellness Policy Supplement: Managing Chronic Conditions (NASN)</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/school-health-conditions/chronic-conditions/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Centers for Disease Control and Prevention: Managing Chronic Health Conditions in Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://showmeschoolhealth.org/resources/gastrostomy-tubes/\">University of Missouri Gastrostomy Tube Resource</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1QqSlUJZ3GkeIJSuzw10eSXo62759Jo-K\">Sample Individualized Health Plans (MASN)</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://learn.nasn.org/courses/25340\">Improving Care Coordination for Students with Chronic Conditions Toolkit (NASN)</a></li>\r\n\t<li><a href=\"https://cdn.fs.pathlms.com/JVYoBzgT5isb2rXqQI5V\">Translating Strategies into Actions to Improve Care Coordination for Students with Chronic Health Conditions</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-align-center\">\r\n<div class=\"text-align-center\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-align-center\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"man breathing\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"f23940cb-1d31-4123-83eb-4c50501f8e9a\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-kelvin-valerio-810775.jpg\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h5 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Asthma</h5>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"50b7990d-c422-4780-a7cd-6885f8a34952\" filename=\"Asthma_Guidelines_FINAL_APPROVED_6_2023_1.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Asthma_Guidelines_FINAL_APPROVED_6_2023_1.pdf\" target=\"_self\" title=\"Guidelines for Maine Schools\">Asthma Management: Guidelines for Maine Schools</a></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Asthma%20Interview%20%5BEnglish%5D%20-%208.21.2024.docx\">Sample Asthma Interview</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong>NASN Resources</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"2d923c11-c4ce-40d5-9578-ca221fe141d0\" filename=\"School Health Services - NASN Asthma Clinical Practice Guidelines - 11.13.2025.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Asthma%20Clinical%20Practice%20Guidelines%20-%2011.13.2025.pdf\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Asthma</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" filename=\"Nurse Checklist 2023.pdf\" href=\"https://higherlogicdownload.s3.amazonaws.com/NASN/3870c72d-fff9-4ed7-833f-215de278d256/UploadedImages/PDFs/Practice%20Topic%20Resources/2015_asthma_care_checklist.pdf\" title=\"Nurse Checklist\">NASN Nurse Checklist</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Other Resources</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/mecdc/diseases-conditions/chronic-conditions/asthma\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Maine CDC Asthma Program\">Maine CDC Asthma Program</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/school-health-conditions/chronic/asthma.html\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC: Managing&nbsp;Asthma in Schools&nbsp;</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.lung.org/lung-health-diseases/lung-disease-lookup/asthma/managing-asthma/children-and-asthma/conversation-guide\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">American Lung Association – 8 Conversations to Have That Are Important for my Child's Asthma Care</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.lung.org/lung-health-diseases/wellness/back-to-school\">American Lung Association - Back to School with Healthy Lungs</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.airnow.gov/\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">AIR Now – Air Quality Flag Program</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/iaq-schools\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">US Environmental Protection Agency – Creating Healthy Indoor Air Quality in Schools</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"Card image cap\" class=\"card-img-top\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/School%20Health%20-%20Chronic%20Conditions%20Diabetes.png\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h5 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Diabetes</h5>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"b17d9329-0365-40d4-95a1-7b58e75ca8e6\" filename=\"School Health Services - Diabetes Management in Maine Schools - 5.19.2026.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Diabetes%20Management%20in%20Maine%20Schools%20-%205.19.2026.pdf\">Diabetes Management: Guidelines for Maine Schools</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Diabetes%20Interview%20%5BEnglish%5D%20-%208.21.2024.docx\">Sample Diabetes Interview</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong>NASN Resources</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/2024-09/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20-%20School%20Nursing%20Evidence-Based%20Clinical%20Practice%20Guideline%20Students%20with%20Type%201%20Diabetes%20-%203.2022.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"National Association of School Nurses (NASN) School Nursing Evidence-Based Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Type 1 Diabetes\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Type 1 Diabetes</a></strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Other Resources</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/caring/managing-diabetes-at-school.html\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC: Managing Diabetes in Schools</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" filename=\"School Health Services - American Diabetes Association - Guidance for the Use of Continuos Glucose Monitoring in School Setting - 6.20.2024_0.pdf\" href=\"https://diabetes.org/sites/default/files/2025-06/CGM-Guidance-06-10-25.pdf\" title=\"American Diabetes Association: Guidance for the Use of Continuous Glucose Monitoring in School Setting\">American Diabetes Association - Guidance for the Use of Continuous Glucose Monitoring in School Setting</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"couple in bed man giving woman water\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"2f94af85-5954-4f03-80a8-d827480266fa\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-pavel-danilyuk-6753343%20%281%29.jpg\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h5 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Seizure Disorder</h5>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong><a data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"0edc789e-9e90-412f-8f7a-cff9bbbc4a03\" filename=\"FINAL Guidelines for Seizure Management_2.9.2023.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/FINAL%20Guidelines%20for%20Seizure%20Management_2.9.2023.pdf\" title=\"Final Guidelines for Seizure Management \">Seizure &amp; Epilepsy Management: Guidelines for Maine Schools</a></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Seizure%20Interview%20%5BEnglish%5D%20-%208.21.2024.docx\">Sample Seizure Interview</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong>NASN Resources</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"b2ff26cd-6562-4144-a4cf-5d5b95993b8b\" filename=\"School Health Services - NASN Seizures and Epilepsy Toolkit - 2023.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Seizures%20and%20Epilepsy%20Toolkit%20-%202023.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Seizures and Epilepsy</a></strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Other Resources</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/school-health-conditions/chronic/epilepsy.html\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC: Managing Epilepsy in Schools</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/epilepsy/php/guidance-for-schools/?CDC_AAref_Val=https://www.cdc.gov/epilepsy/groups/professionals.htm\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC Training Materials</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://learn.nasn.org/courses/63321\" target=\"_blank\">NASN School Nursing Evidence-Based Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Seizures and Epilepsy</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.epilepsy.com/preparedness-safety\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Epilepsy Foundation Preparedness</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"allergy medication bottle\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"a95eabb6-5b50-4791-b8c6-1d51c7440a09\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-cottonbro-studio-6865181%20%281%29.jpg\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h5 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Life-threatening Allergy</h5>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"a804765f-3ba1-4b77-b358-57e65736acc4\" filename=\"School Health Services - NASN Allergy and Anaphylaxis Clinical Practice Guidelines - 11.13.2025.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Allergy%20and%20Anaphylaxis%20Clinical%20Practice%20Guidelines%20-%2011.13.2025.pdf\"><strong>NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Allergies and Risk for Anaphylaxis</strong></a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a class=\"file file--mime-application-pdf file--application-pdf\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"9ffc39bf-4f54-47db-82fc-8cd5d53e99d2\" filename=\"School Health Services - NASN Allergy and Anaphylaxis Toolkit - 11.13.2025.pdf\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Allergy%20and%20Anaphylaxis%20Toolkit%20-%2011.13.2025.pdf\">NASN Allergy &amp; Anaphylaxis Toolkit</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\">\r\n\t<p><a class=\"file file--mime-application-vnd-openxmlformats-officedocument-wordprocessingml-document file--x-office-document\" data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"7d30b8eb-5bf7-4927-917e-f13121d76ff2\" filename=\"School Health Services - Food Allergy Management in Schools (FAMS)– 9.2024.docx\" href=\"https://www.foodallergy.org/resources/food-allergy-management-schools-fams-expert-recommendations-k-12\">Food Allergy Management in Schools (FAMS): Expert Recommendations for K-12</a></p>\r\n\t</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.aaaai.org/tools-for-the-public/school-tools/anaphylaxis-food-allergy/stock-epinephrine\" target=\"_blank\">American Academy of Allergy Asthma &amp; Immunology: Stock Epinephrine Toolkit for Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.kyahraynefoundation.org/\">Kyah Rayne Foundation</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20AAP%20Allergy%20and%20Anaphylaxis%20Emergency%20Plan%20-%202017.pdf\">American Academy of Pediatrics Allergy and Anaphylaxis Emergency Plan</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a data-entity-type=\"file\" data-entity-uuid=\"d41c6f0a-9b7f-4123-bc18-afbf54ae264c\" filename=\"School Health Services - Sample Collaborative Practice Agreement - 2.26.2025 .docx\" href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Collaborative%20Practice%20Agreement%20-%202.26.2025%20.docx\">Sample Collaborative Practice Agreement</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Schools may utilize programs to assist in supplying a stock of Epinephrine</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.epipen4schools.com/\" target=\"_blank\">EpiPen4Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.neffy.com/community-programs/\" tabindex=\"-1\"><em>neffy</em>inSchools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://convenientmd.com/schoolnurses/\" target=\"_blank\">Convenient MD School Nurse Partnership</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3 class=\"text-align-left\"><strong>Contact</strong></h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"text-align-left\" paraeid=\"{b4edfa76-4015-45cf-ab3a-0d78f41ceee6}{184}\" paraid=\"803522662\"><strong>Emily Poland, MPH, RN,&nbsp;NCSN&nbsp;</strong><br />\r\nSchool Nurse Consultant<br />\r\nCoordinated School Health Team Leader<br />\r\n<strong>Email</strong>: <a href=\"mailto:emily.poland@maine.gov\">emily.poland@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n","after":"<div class=\"doe-hero doe-hero--tall\">\n<p class=\"doe-contact-link\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-lead\">Students with chronic conditions often have unique educational needs and health considerations that require individual planning. Every student with a chronic condition should have access to school nursing care. Better management and control of chronic health conditions are key, leading to success for these students, both in school and in their community. Care for these students should include teaching and encouraging self-care skills, as the locus of control for making decisions about health shifts to the individual.</p>\n\n</div>\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>To help schools eliminate discrimination against students with disabilities due to chronic conditions or other reasons, the Office of Civil Rights created this resource: <a href=\"https://www.ed.gov/media/document/parent-and-educator-resource-guide-section-504-public-elementary-and-secondary-schools-2016-21262.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Parent and Educator Guide to Section 504</a>. Many students with chronic conditions will qualify for accommodations through Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973.&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-12\">\r\n<div class=\"card\">\r\n<div class=\"card-header text-white bg-primary\"><strong>Chronic Conditions Resources</strong></div>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://cdn.fs.pathlms.com/GtkmrVvSy64YFX7jL4Yh?cache=true\" target=\"_blank\">School Wellness Policy Supplement: Managing Chronic Conditions (NASN)</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/school-health-conditions/chronic-conditions/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Centers for Disease Control and Prevention: Managing Chronic Health Conditions in Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://showmeschoolhealth.org/resources/gastrostomy-tubes/\" target=\"_blank\">University of Missouri Gastrostomy Tube Resource</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/u/0/folders/1QqSlUJZ3GkeIJSuzw10eSXo62759Jo-K\" target=\"_blank\">Sample Individualized Health Plans (MASN)</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://learn.nasn.org/courses/25340\" target=\"_blank\">Improving Care Coordination for Students with Chronic Conditions Toolkit (NASN)</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action\"><a href=\"https://cdn.fs.pathlms.com/JVYoBzgT5isb2rXqQI5V\" target=\"_blank\">Translating Strategies into Actions to Improve Care Coordination for Students with Chronic Health Conditions</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"text-align-center\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"man breathing\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-kelvin-valerio-810775.jpg\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h3 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Asthma</h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action card-text text-align-left\"><strong><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/Asthma_Guidelines_FINAL_APPROVED_6_2023_1.pdf\" title=\"Guidelines for Maine Schools\">Asthma Management: Guidelines for Maine Schools</a></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Asthma%20Interview%20%5BEnglish%5D%20-%208.21.2024.docx\">Sample Asthma Interview</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong>NASN Resources</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Asthma%20Clinical%20Practice%20Guidelines%20-%2011.13.2025.pdf\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Asthma</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://higherlogicdownload.s3.amazonaws.com/NASN/3870c72d-fff9-4ed7-833f-215de278d256/UploadedImages/PDFs/Practice%20Topic%20Resources/2015_asthma_care_checklist.pdf\" title=\"Nurse Checklist\" target=\"_blank\">NASN Nurse Checklist</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Other Resources</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/mecdc/diseases-conditions/chronic-conditions/asthma\" title=\"Maine CDC Asthma Program\">Maine CDC Asthma Program</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/school-health-conditions/chronic/asthma.html\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC: Managing&nbsp;Asthma in Schools</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.lung.org/lung-health-diseases/lung-disease-lookup/asthma/managing-asthma/children-and-asthma/conversation-guide\" target=\"_blank\">American Lung Association – 8 Conversations to Have That Are Important for my Child's Asthma Care</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.lung.org/lung-health-diseases/wellness/back-to-school\" target=\"_blank\">American Lung Association - Back to School with Healthy Lungs</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.airnow.gov/\" target=\"_blank\">AIR Now – Air Quality Flag Program</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.epa.gov/iaq-schools\" target=\"_blank\">US Environmental Protection Agency – Creating Healthy Indoor Air Quality in Schools</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"Card image cap\" class=\"card-img-top\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/School%20Health%20-%20Chronic%20Conditions%20Diabetes.png\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h3 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Diabetes</h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Diabetes%20Management%20in%20Maine%20Schools%20-%205.19.2026.pdf\">Diabetes Management: Guidelines for Maine Schools</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Diabetes%20Interview%20%5BEnglish%5D%20-%208.21.2024.docx\">Sample Diabetes Interview</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong>NASN Resources</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/2024-09/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20-%20School%20Nursing%20Evidence-Based%20Clinical%20Practice%20Guideline%20Students%20with%20Type%201%20Diabetes%20-%203.2022.pdf\" title=\"National Association of School Nurses (NASN) School Nursing Evidence-Based Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Type 1 Diabetes\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Type 1 Diabetes</a></strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Other Resources</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/diabetes/caring/managing-diabetes-at-school.html\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC: Managing Diabetes in Schools</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://diabetes.org/sites/default/files/2025-06/CGM-Guidance-06-10-25.pdf\" title=\"American Diabetes Association: Guidance for the Use of Continuous Glucose Monitoring in School Setting\" target=\"_blank\">American Diabetes Association - Guidance for the Use of Continuous Glucose Monitoring in School Setting</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"row justify-content-center\">\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"couple in bed man giving woman water\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-pavel-danilyuk-6753343%20%281%29.jpg\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h3 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Seizure Disorder</h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action card-text text-align-left\"><strong><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/FINAL%20Guidelines%20for%20Seizure%20Management_2.9.2023.pdf\" title=\"Final Guidelines for Seizure Management \">Seizure &amp; Epilepsy Management: Guidelines for Maine Schools</a></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"doe-action card-text text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Seizure%20Interview%20%5BEnglish%5D%20-%208.21.2024.docx\">Sample Seizure Interview</a></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"card-text text-align-left\"><strong>NASN Resources</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Seizures%20and%20Epilepsy%20Toolkit%20-%202023.pdf\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Seizures and Epilepsy</a></strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Other Resources</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/school-health-conditions/chronic/epilepsy.html\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC: Managing Epilepsy in Schools</a>&nbsp;</li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/epilepsy/php/guidance-for-schools/?CDC_AAref_Val=https://www.cdc.gov/epilepsy/groups/professionals.htm\" target=\"_blank\">US CDC Training Materials</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://learn.nasn.org/courses/63321\" target=\"_blank\">NASN School Nursing Evidence-Based Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Seizures and Epilepsy</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.epilepsy.com/preparedness-safety\" target=\"_blank\">Epilepsy Foundation Preparedness</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div class=\"col-sm-6\">\r\n<div class=\"card\"><img alt=\"allergy medication bottle\" height=\"100%\" src=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-images/pexels-cottonbro-studio-6865181%20%281%29.jpg\" width=\"100%\" />\r\n<div class=\"card-body\">\r\n<h3 class=\"card-title text-align-left\">Life-threatening Allergy</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul class=\"list-group list-group-flush\">\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Allergy%20and%20Anaphylaxis%20Clinical%20Practice%20Guidelines%20-%2011.13.2025.pdf\">NASN Clinical Practice Guideline: Students with Allergies and Risk for Anaphylaxis</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20NASN%20Allergy%20and%20Anaphylaxis%20Toolkit%20-%2011.13.2025.pdf\">NASN Allergy &amp; Anaphylaxis Toolkit</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.foodallergy.org/resources/food-allergy-management-schools-fams-expert-recommendations-k-12\" target=\"_blank\">Food Allergy Management in Schools (FAMS): Expert Recommendations for K-12</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.aaaai.org/tools-for-the-public/school-tools/anaphylaxis-food-allergy/stock-epinephrine\" target=\"_blank\">American Academy of Allergy Asthma &amp; Immunology: Stock Epinephrine Toolkit for Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.kyahraynefoundation.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Kyah Rayne Foundation</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.maine.gov/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20AAP%20Allergy%20and%20Anaphylaxis%20Emergency%20Plan%20-%202017.pdf\">American Academy of Pediatrics Allergy and Anaphylaxis Emergency Plan</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"/doe/sites/maine.gov.doe/files/inline-files/School%20Health%20Services%20-%20Sample%20Collaborative%20Practice%20Agreement%20-%202.26.2025%20.docx\">Sample Collaborative Practice Agreement</a><span class=\"doe-chip\" data-src=\"file\">Word</span></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"list-group-item text-align-left\"><strong>Schools may utilize programs to assist in supplying a stock of Epinephrine</strong></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.epipen4schools.com/\" target=\"_blank\">EpiPen4Schools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://www.neffy.com/community-programs/\" target=\"_blank\"><em>neffy</em>inSchools</a></li>\r\n\t<li class=\"doe-action list-group-item text-align-left\"><a href=\"https://convenientmd.com/schoolnurses/\" target=\"_blank\">Convenient MD School Nurse Partnership</a></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div id=\"contact\" class=\"contact-cube\">\r\n<h3 class=\"text-align-left\">Contact</h3>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"text-align-left\"><strong>Emily Poland, MPH, RN,&nbsp;NCSN&nbsp;</strong><br />\r\n<em>School Nurse Consultant</em><br />\r\nCoordinated School Health Team Leader<br />\r\n<strong>Email</strong>: <a href=\"mailto:emily.poland@maine.gov\">Emily.Poland@maine.gov</a></p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\n<p class=\"doe-jump\"><a href=\"#contact\">Contact</a></p>\n<p class=\"doe-top\"><a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a></p>","notes":["452 words with no section headers at all — the biggest single improvement available here."],"decisions":[{"id":"emailcase","on":true,"label":"Write the email addresses the same way","why":"1 address is shown in whatever case it was typed in. The house form capitalises each name and leaves a middle initial in lower case — emily.poland@maine.gov → Emily.Poland@maine.gov. Only the first letter of each part changes, so a name that spells itself LaBreck keeps doing so.","value":"1 address"},{"id":"filechip","on":true,"label":"Tag a document link with the format it opens","why":"1 link on this page opens a file — 1 Word — and says nothing about it, while others in the same list carry a tag because their author typed one. The format is read from the file name, so the list stops being half-labelled. No link text changes.","value":"1 link"},{"id":"cardtitles","on":true,"label":"Put the card titles on one level","why":"4 card titles are written at a level copied from an example rather than chosen — h5 on a page whose sections are h2. Only the number changes.","value":"4 titles"},{"id":"contacttitle","on":true,"label":"Set a job title the way the rest of the site does","why":"1 job title sits in plain text under the person's name, where 186 elsewhere on the site are in italics — so the same contact block is drawn two ways depending on the page, and the title runs into the name above it. The standard here is the site's own, not a preference: two thirds of these blocks already do it. No word changes.","value":"1 title"},{"id":"deck","on":true,"label":"Use this paragraph as the page description","why":"It is the page’s own opening paragraph, moved into the banner rather than rewritten.","value":"Students with chronic conditions often have unique educational needs and health considerations that require individual planning. Every student with a chronic condition should have access to school nursing care. Better management and control of chronic health conditions are key, leading to success for these students, both in school and in their community. Care for these students should include teaching and encouraging self-care skills, as the locus of control for making decisions about health shifts to the individual."},{"id":"banner-graphic","on":true,"label":"Retire the old banner graphic","why":"It repeats the page title in picture form, which the new banner already does in type.","removes":"School Health - Chronic Conditions Web Banner.png"}],"mechanical":["empty paragraphs removed: 2","drupal entity attrs stripped: 49","target set by destination: 25","paragraph inside a list item unwrapped: 1","loose text wrapped in a paragraph: 1","redundant bold inside a heading removed: 1","empty divs removed: 2","paragraph unwrapped inside a card header: 1","margin utilities removed from card headers: 1","emphasis removed from inside a link: 1","action links marked: 38","space moved out of a link: 1"],"findings":[{"name":"card-row-holding-one-card","n":1,"eg":["a grid row with one card in it"]}],"safe":true,"audit":{"alias":"/schools/safeschools/healthed/nurseresources/manual/chronic","title":"Guidelines for School